        null
    ],
    "optionsVersion": 1,
    "apiVersion": "VERSION_0",
    "isResourceIntensiveScript": false,
    "showPartitioning": false,
    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "HHI, Gini, top-N and top-20% shares and Lorenz curves for customer, supplier or market concentration, per group.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Finance",
    "tags": [
        "concentration",
        "HHI",
        "Herfindahl",
        "Gini",
        "Lorenz curve",
        "market share",
        "supplier risk",
        "customer concentration",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Measures **how concentrated a total is** among the entities that make it up: customers in revenue, suppliers in spend, firms in a market, products in sales, overall and per group (market, region, year).\n\n- **HHI** (Herfindahl-Hirschman index: sum of squared percentage shares, 0 to 10,000), normalised HHI and the **equivalent number of equal-sized entities**\n- **Gini coefficient** and the **Lorenz curve** (101 points per group, ready to chart against the equality line)\n- **Top-1, top-4 (CR4) and top-10 shares**, the share held by the **top 20%** of entities, and how many entities make up **50% and 80%** of the total\n- An **HHI band** with thresholds you can set (defaults 1,500 and 2,500, the bands used in the 2010 US Horizontal Merger Guidelines)\n\nValues are summed per entity first; entities with zero or negative totals are left out. Outputs: the measures per group, the Lorenz curve, and each entity with share, rank and cumulative share.",
    "dependencies": "",
